    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>This plugin provides controls to disable JavaScript and CSS files enqueued by themes and plugins.</p>\n<p><strong>Features:</strong><br />\n*   Global Settings: Disable assets across the frontend or by specific post type.<br />\n*   Per-Post Settings: Disable assets individually on specific Pages, Posts, or Custom Post Types.<br />\n*   Grouped View: Assets are grouped by Plugin, Theme, or Core.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the <code>mcod-disable-enqueue-js-css</code> folder to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; menu in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Go to Settings &gt; Disable Assets to configure global settings.</li>\n<li>Edit any post/page to configure local settings.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.2.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Selectively disable enqueued JS and CSS files.",
